NET - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

Messages over the primary modem (network or
wireless card), and host names. See also
NETWORKING.md.

net.modem() -> proxy

The primary modem, or nil if there is no network
or wireless card.

net.open(port) -> boolean

Opens a port on the primary modem (1–65535).
Errors if there is no modem.

net.close([port]) -> boolean

Closes a port, or all ports.

net.send(address, port, ...) -> boolean

Sends a message to one modem. Values: nil,
booleans, numbers, strings (8 values, 8 KiB in
total).

net.broadcast(port, ...) -> boolean

Sends a message to every modem in reach.

net.receive([timeout[, port]]) -> from, port, distance, ...

Waits for a message (on one port, or any open
port). Returns the sender's address, the port, the
distance and the values, or nil after the timeout.

  net.open(5)
  local from, port, distance, text = net.receive(10, 5)

net.hostname() -> string

This computer's host name (os.hostname()).

net.discover([hostname[, timeout]]) -> table

Broadcasts a lookup on port 1 and collects answers
for timeout seconds (default 1). Returns a list of
{address, hostname, distance}. Only computers
running the beacon service (enabled by default)
answer; with a host name, only that host answers.

net.resolve(name[, timeout]) -> address

The address of a host by name (a full address is
returned as is), or nil.
